eles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry/high season; driest reef water, own rates peak)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off winter, layered on structural ~20-30% vs Playa del Carmen)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane season, ~40-60% off; reef/cenote year-round, dry-season visibility best)","booking_lead":"shoulder/green beds 2-4 wks; reef/cenote tours 1-3 wks; Dec-Apr beds + Zoëtry/Royalton Reserve ultra suite 3-6+ months (more for Christmas/NY)","off_season_specials":"double-discount play - ''cheaper than Cancún AND low season''; pair value bed with year-round national-park reef + weather-resilient Route of the Cenotes; disclose hurricane/sargassum","event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, US spring break (Mar); no single marquee wildlife event - reef + cenotes are the year-round draw","fire_date":"winter/value-vs-Cancún Aug-Sep; green-season ''cheaper base + cenotes'' Apr-May; ultra corridor (Mayakoba/Zoëtry) 6-9 months ahead"},"jewels":[{"name":"Juan Escutia wreck","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"sunken boat now an artificial reef and fish refuge","bookable_category":"guided reef/wreck dive","source":"https://www.kooxdiving.com/en/activiti